WEBVTT

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.580
So, this is the Splinter of Knowledge...

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:37.820
This thing took your power and...

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:44.610
This Splinter of Knowledge...
No, the "Arcanum of the Craft"...

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.630
What the hell is it?

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.710
Why did you have it?

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.170
Nagira... There are some things that even I don't have the answers to.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.930
To be honest, I don't know if returning this to you is such a good idea.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:14.470
I'll admit that this thing's power saved my life.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.600
But on the other hand, I may end up the same as that guy if you suddenly felt like it.

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:24.140
The thought of one human having such incredible power gives me the willies.

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:29.380
Can you control it? Can you control this power?

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.980
Well, can you?

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:37.630
I don't know for sure, either.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.930
There are some people I want to introduce you to.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:44.600
They might know something about this.

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:47.490
Let me talk to them.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.730
I feel like it'll disappear...

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:07.460
...the instant I look away.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.600
I just kept counting...

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:18.040
...all the many traces of loneliness...

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:25.410
...that I'd vomited up.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:31.350
In this time that seems so dry,

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:36.460
...my heart is thrashing around and drowning.

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:42.320
It takes those lies that make my head spin...

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:45.370
...and tears them to pieces.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:55.040
 And the place I lose my way in...

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:02.870
...is a dim, hazy world.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:30.260
Sorry to make you come all the way out here.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:35.110
This is the girl I told you about...

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.080
I'm Robin.

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:39.340
My name is Kannosaki.

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:42.980
This is my wife...

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:45.950
Hey.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:48.750
Pleased to meet you.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.720
This is it.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:56.760
I'd heard there was an object that could bestow the inner secrets to a Witch, but I...

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.700
May I touch it?

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.160
Hm? Sure.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:10.440
What do you think? I had heard that you two were well-versed in Witchcraft.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:13.470
Well, it just turned out that way.

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:17.920
I believe my wife might know more about this than I do.

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:22.120
Hitomi, have you seen anything like this in the library?

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:24.960
Hitomi?

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:25.960
Yes?

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:27.090
Have you seen this?

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:31.260
I'm sorry, I've never seen it before.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:33.930
I'm terribly sorry.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.300
No, that's quite all right.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:39.830
I would, however, ask that you not discuss this matter with anyone else.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.800
We understand completely.

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.550
We want to lead a quiet, peaceful life, too.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:48.380
It looks like we won't be of much help.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:49.440
We should be going.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.010
Hitomi.

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:54.010
I'm sorry.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:58.760
Well, we're off.

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:01.690
If you ever need any help with anything, give me a call.

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:03.290
Thank you, we will.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.100
That's too bad.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.280
Well, sometimes coming up empty can be for the best.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.340
Don't worry about it.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:22.580
Nagira, do I have something on my face?

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:23.280
Hm?

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:27.120
That woman was staring at me.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.490
Are you sure you weren't imagining things?

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.720
Really, she was!

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.460
You're just being self-conscious.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:33.620
It's not that.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.680
Want to see you.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.680
Will be waiting

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.680
at usual place.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.500
Hm? Hey!

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:42.470
Sorry.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:44.940
I'm heading out for a bit.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.940
Pachinko again, sir?!

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:48.570
Hey, this is important business.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:50.910
You have an appointment for this evening, so...

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.010
Yeah, yeah... I know.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:09.960
What have you got for me?

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:15.960
I heard a rumor that there's a guy who worked as an errand boy for old lady Methuselah.

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:22.110
I figure that if anybody knows about that splinter, it's him.

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:25.210
They call him Lazarus.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:30.110
They say the old lady brought him back to life just as he was about to die,

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:32.080
...so that's why they gave him that nickname.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:35.920
But I hear that nobody's seen him around lately,

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:39.190
...so if you're looking for him, you might want to hurry.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.770
Amon? But how...

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:55.680
Amon!

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:11.590
Robin!

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:14.420
You've got a call from the wife who was here yesterday.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:17.730
Are you still sleeping?

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.260
If you don't come down, I'm hanging up.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:23.300
You have 10 seconds.

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:24.100
Nine!

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:25.470
Eight!

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.040
Okay, I've got it. I'll be right there.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:36.650
Where's Nagira?

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:39.190
He hasn't been back since he took off.

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:41.250
Darn it, where's he off goofing around THIS time?

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:42.790
Maybe he's at his girlfriend's.

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:43.620
Huh?

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:45.550
Somebody said they wanted to meet him.

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:48.730
Oh, geez... I didn't think about that!

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:51.600
That was so stupid of me!

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.000
I really need to keep a close eye on him!

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:54.000
I'm going out for a bit.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:57.660
I wish he'd stop drinking, gambling, and womanizing during office hours.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:02.640
Um...

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:05.110
It's open! Please, come on in.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:06.640
All right.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:11.310
I'm so glad you came!

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.110
Make yourself at home.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:15.820
Um...

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:19.120
I'll make some tea. Do you like black tea?

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:20.590
Sure...

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.060
I received some wonderful black tea a while ago.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:29.240
But my husband doesn't notice these things, so there's no point in making it.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:30.370
Um...

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:35.040
Would you like something sweet?
I made your favorite orange cake.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:40.180
Listen, about the Splinter...

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:42.080
Oh, could you wait a moment?

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:50.450
Sorry about that.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:56.260
Look, this is the one piece dress that you said that you wanted.

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:58.400
Good thing I got a size 9, huh?

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:00.200
Stop that, Hitomi.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.060
Honey...

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.070
Just give it a rest.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:09.070
That girl isn't Aya.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:12.070
What are you doing here?

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:15.410
She said that she remembered something about the Splinter.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.420
Could I have a word with you alone?

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.120
This is our daughter's room.

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.930
It's not used anymore.

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:29.490
What happened to her?

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:33.300
Chances are that she was hunted.

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:37.830
Aya was a Witch.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.170
My wife thought you...

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:44.770
I'm sorry.

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:48.310
I've heard about you from Mr. Nagira.

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:51.050
This place is under surveillance.

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:53.710
You shouldn't associate with us anymore.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.630
We've been expecting you.

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:49.470
What's been going on at Solomon headquarters since the attack?

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:51.340
No activity whatsoever.

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:54.310
Perhaps they're waiting to see what move we will make.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:57.380
I doubt they give us that much credit.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:00.990
Rumors are circulating that the attack on the STN-J...

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:03.750
...means that Solomon headquarters has cut you loose.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.660
If any more of these negative rumors get around,

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:10.060
there's a chance that we'll even lose our sponsors.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:12.330
You want to replace me right away, do you?

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:13.370
No, sir.

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:18.700
What I'm trying to say is that perhaps you should avoid any overt activity for a while.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:22.910
The STN-J is safe for now, but if this place were attacked...

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:28.210
Director, your real motivating factor is that you value your life, yes?

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:33.310
You don't seem to understand this, Director, but this place is a fortress.

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:37.860
No one could take this place easily, not even Solomon headquarters.

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:38.830
But...

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:41.720
It's time to make a decision.

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:44.390
We will speed up the project.

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:47.640
B-But that's...

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:53.000
Solomon's views will have to change once they see the results of the evolved Orbo.

00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:56.570
We will no longer need Witches' powers on hunts.

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:00.440
Now is the time to take that first step towards our ideal.

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:03.010
What's our development status?

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:07.160
We're getting results of 97% in our simulations.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:10.850
Once you give us authorization to gather data in live combat, we can move out at any time.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:15.030
You have authorization. I'll forward the STN-J's hunt list to you.

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:17.530
Begin your preparations.

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:19.300
Understood.

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:21.590
I expect to see more efficient results this time.

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:01.670
Huh?

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:05.040
Why am I crying...?

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:21.160
Oops! That was close...

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:24.690
Geez, is this guy really down...

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:27.990
Is that the place?

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:33.000
Lazarus?

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:36.700
You awake?

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:39.910
Beg pardon...

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:45.920
Crap!

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:01.260
If you're gonna kill me, come on and kill me!

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:14.920
Just a warning, huh?

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:21.550
I'm sending you my dry cleaning bill, Amon!

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:29.460
What are you doing here?

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:31.090
I was in the area.

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:32.720
You!

00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:36.130
I'd like to talk some more.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:38.870
Come in!

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.500
She can come in, right, honey?

00:14:44.180 --> 00:14:46.510
I was just starting dinner.

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:48.280
Is there anything that you don't like?

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:50.520
No, not really.

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:53.150
Really? I'll go all-out, then!

00:15:00.130 --> 00:15:01.120
Thank you.

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:06.790
It seems like it's been forever since I last saw her this happy.

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:11.340
She had been crying ever since you left yesterday, you see.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:15.300
No, ever since our daughter disappeared.

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:19.750
Maybe I've just been pretending not to notice.

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:24.880
I guess it's because there's nothing I can do.

00:15:27.490 --> 00:15:30.720
Would you mind if I asked about Aya?

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:36.650
Three years ago, her powers awakened.

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:40.600
They were weak, hardly enough to make a pencil roll around.

00:15:42.070 --> 00:15:44.540
We used every means at our disposal to find out...

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:47.630
...if we could make this unwanted power go away.

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:50.540
But in the end, we were never able to find a way.

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:57.810
And then one day, she went to school, and we haven't seen her since.

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:03.360
We, who are called "Seeds" by the STN-J, are always watched by someone.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:06.430
And if we show signs of powers, however faint,

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:09.230
...we're ratted out, and our very existence is erased.

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:11.730
Did you look for her?

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:14.430
We looked everywhere. For months.

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:17.630
We even asked the media and the police for help.

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:19.840
But they all ignored us.

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:25.110
The only one who offered a helping hand was Mr. Nagira.

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:30.820
Right up until the morning she disappeared,

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:34.350
...my wife had been fighting with her over buying a new dress.

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:38.250
She's regretted not buying it for her ever since.

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:45.260
I'm sorry, I've neglected to entertain you.

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:47.120
Um... I'll help you.

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:51.700
Thank you. But do you think you could do something else for me?

00:16:57.710 --> 00:16:59.580
I wonder if she'll like this?

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:00.740
She might.

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:15.930
Honey...! How long have you...

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:20.230
I'm sorry. I might not be around for much longer now.

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:27.940
My, Mr. Nagira, you're certainly back early.

00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:29.240
Yeah.

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:31.370
What do you mean, "Yeah"? Pee-yew!

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:34.420
Mr. Nagira, where did you pick up that stench?!

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:35.280
I'll send that right out to the cleaners, so...

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.010
Where's Robin?

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:38.280
She went to see that couple from yesterday.

00:17:39.090 --> 00:17:40.250
What did you say?

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:52.330
They tell me you'll be able to leave soon.

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:57.940
Where's Amon?

00:17:57.940 --> 00:18:00.570
Don't go after him. Just forget him.

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:03.140
What do you plan to do with him?

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.650
He's different from us.

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:07.110
He's human.

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:11.540
I have a duty to preserve the purity of humanity.

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:17.980
I've put together everything you'll need.

00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:22.560
Go make a new life for yourself, Touko.

00:18:29.300 --> 00:18:31.460
I'm sorry for dropping by unannounced.

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:34.130
I'd like you to have this dress.

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:37.330
That's all right. I'll drop by again sometime.

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:39.410
Yes, you're right.

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:43.450
I'll see you later.

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:14.010
I forgot my...

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:25.720
Do you suppose she'll stop by again?

00:19:25.960 --> 00:19:28.360
It's all right, honey. I'm sure she...

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:33.730
Hitomi, escape out the back.

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:35.030
I won't run.

00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:44.240
I don't want to lose anyone else.

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:46.310
Hitomi...

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:27.680
It can't be...

00:20:29.090 --> 00:20:30.350
But they were just...

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:31.960
Robin!

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:33.720
What are you...

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:39.730
Nagira... They're gone.

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:44.740
Those people, they...

00:20:45.940 --> 00:20:48.740
Those people, they're gone...!

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:02.110
And?

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:07.790
I was sent to Japan by Solomon headquarters to retrieve the Arcanum of the Craft.

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:13.000
Working as a hunter at the STN-J was camouflage for that mission.

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:18.540
In other words, nobody outside of headquarters was supposed to know, huh?

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:24.540
I retrieve the Arcanum, hand it over to a messenger from headquarters,

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:27.040
...and my mission ends there.

00:21:27.980 --> 00:21:29.750
This mission was supposed to work that way, too.

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:31.080
But...

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:40.090
But this mission didn't go like that.

00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:43.660
So the attack on the STN-J wasn't because of the Arcanum?

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:46.690
If they wanted it, all they had to do was wait for me to give it to them.

00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:51.000
So you really don't know what's hidden in this thing?

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:59.270
I was only assigned to retrieve it.

00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:03.920
I didn't need to know what was in it.

00:22:10.690 --> 00:22:13.720
Nagira... Look after that for me.

00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:18.560
Hey, this is your ace in the hole.

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:21.070
I know that.

00:22:22.140 --> 00:22:27.630
But right now... I know I won't be able to keep that power in check.

00:22:36.980 --> 00:22:44.970
Just how far back do I need to go?

00:22:44.790 --> 00:22:47.830
Tell me.

00:22:49.040 --> 00:22:59.820
It's all so vivid that it hurts.

00:23:00.680 --> 00:23:09.710
The truth is, nothing can be shared,

00:23:09.390 --> 00:23:14.200
...so I never looked back.

00:23:15.470 --> 00:23:19.570
...all those promises...

00:23:21.510 --> 00:23:25.970
...inside me eventually...

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:31.770
...gave up on that light from some other time,

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:40.550
...like the light of a morning you can't return to.
